Z||000000||PAUL88GT||01-23-2001||07:36 PM||||This e-bay auction seems to indicate that people are willing to pay higher prices, sight unseen in some cases:<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=544175709&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=544175709&r=0&t=0</A> <P>What is your observation?<P>Also noticed there are 10 pages of Fiero e-bay auctions. I have never seen it this high before. Usually 5-6 pages.<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||Kelvin Vivian||01-23-2001||08:16 PM||||I took a look at that 88 GT earlier on EBay, all I have to say is that is one BEAUTIFUL car... It looks nice spoilerless, it has a clean look. <P>I recently paid $2026.00 on EBay for the car pictured in my signature... I would have paid more since I was looking for this particular model Fiero since it's kind of like an 84 Indy Fiero, and there weren't too many 87 SE 4-cyls produced. But gladly the price topped off where it did. I believe the price of Fieros will continue upward, especially for nice, clean Fieros that have been taken care of, no matter what year or model.<P>I was kind of hesistant of buying the car off EBay, sight unseen, but then again, it was listed with lots of pictures. And the owner was the original owner and had maintained all the records of what was done to the car.<P>There's a nice grey 85 SE 4-cyl, automatic with low miles listed on EBay, however, it has an engine knock...<P>Fieros are FUN!<BR>Kelvin<BR>87 SE - Med Red Met ext./Grey Int., 4-cyl, 5-spd, spoiler, sunroof, subwoofer, manual windows, manual locks, manual mirrors, AC, (Currently has 15in Grey GT Rims on it, with 205/55 size tires).<BR>88 GT - Red ext./Beechwood Int., 5-spd, T-tops, Spoiler, PW, PL, PM, Rear def, AC.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/SouthBeach/Cove/2449/finalfront.jpg">  1987 SE - 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||14
Z||000002||stimpy||01-23-2001||10:45 PM||||Wow, Kelvin, that is one sweet looking SE! I think you got a helluva deal on it if it looked like that when you got it.<P>BTW, whereabouts in SJ are you?  I grew up in the Evergreen area (White Rd & Aborn) before moving to Tracy in 1990. Go Sharks, eh?<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||Kelvin Vivian||04-17-2001||09:29 PM||||I know exactly where you were Stimpy... I grew up in South San Jose, south of Bernal Road off the 101...<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402882&Sequence=2&res=high"> <P>I bought this SE off of eBay from the original owner. She always garaged the car, and as far as what I've done to the car, I've replaced the faded spoiler, with another spoiler that has the original burgundy paint, and I've added the GT rims. You can't tell from the pic, but the front fascia is "pitted" and so it needs a front end paint job. ||||reg||1
